    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d842">

                <pb facs="0781" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.6292/5</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Siam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-05T13:00:00+06:42">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 5, 1917, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 6, 5.15 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs requests me to ascertain if my Government would have
                    any objection to the German and Austrian chargés d’affaires passing through the
                    Pajiama Canal. They intend returning to Europe on the Danish steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Fionia</hi>, leaving here at the end of this month for
                    Copenhagen via Panama Canal. British Government has refused to allow them to go
                    through Suez Canal. Minister for Foreign Affairs asked me to state that he would
                    be glad if objections were made as it would compel chargés d’affaires to take
                    Danish boat <hi rendition="#italic">Falstamd</hi>, leaving Siam about the middle
                    of this month for London via Cape of Good Hope, to which they objected they
                    would be going into the danger zone.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Arnold</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
